{"c": null, "r": "I'm designing a Bank class where each instance maintains its own accounts dictionary. The open_account method validates that the account doesn't already exist and the initial balance is non-negative, raising ValueError if either check fails. For deposits, I need to validate that the amount is positive, then check if the account exists—a missing account should raise KeyError, with validation happening before any mutation.

Withdraw and transfer operations validate the amount, check for account existence, verify the source has sufficient funds, and only then apply the debit and credit. InsufficientFunds inherits from ValueError, and I'll write the file now.
", "t": [["write_file", "{"path":"D:\\Projects\\local_ai\\strata-lab\\runs\\work\\hermes\\bank-1794053343\\bank.py","content":"\"\"\"Account helpers. Balances are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InsufficientFunds(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a withdrawal or transfer exceeds the source balance.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass Bank:\n    \"\"\"A set of accounts. Separate instances never share accounts.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._accounts = {}\n\n    def open_account(self, name, initial=0):\n        if initial < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"initial balance must be >= 0: \" + repr(initial))\n        if name in self._accounts:\n            raise ValueError(\"account exists: \" + name)\n        self._accounts[name] = initial\n\n    def deposit(self, name, amount):\n        self._check_amount(amount)\n        self._get(name)\n        self._accounts[name] += amount\n\n    def withdraw(self, name, amount):\n        self._check_amount(amount)\n        current = self._get(name)\n        if current < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has balance %d, cannot withdraw %d\"\n                % (name, current, amount)\n            )\n        self._accounts[name] = current - amount\n\n    def balance(self, name):\n        return self._get(name)\n\n    def transfer(self, src, dst, amount):\n        self._check_amount(amount)\n        if src == dst:\n            raise ValueError(\"cannot transfer to the same account: \" + src)\n        src_balance = self._get(src)\n        self._get(dst)\n        if src_balance < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"account %r has balance %d, cannot transfer %d to %r\"\n                % (src, src_balance, amount, dst)\n            )\n        self._accounts[src] = src_balance - amount\n        self._accounts[dst] = self._accounts[dst] + amount\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def _check_amount(amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0: \" + repr(amount))\n\n    def _get(self, name):\n        try:\n            return self._accounts[name]\n        except KeyError:\n            raise KeyError(\"unknown account: \" + repr(name))\n\n\ndefault_bank = Bank()\n\n\ndef open_account(name, initial=0):\n    return default_bank.open_account(name, initial)\n\n\ndef deposit(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.deposit(name, amount)\n\n\ndef withdraw(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.withdraw(name, amount)\n\n\ndef balance(name):\n    return default_bank.balance(name)\n\n\ndef transfer(src, dst, amount):\n    return default_bank.transfer(src, dst, amount)\n"}"]]}

